[2] Sixth any-angle carrier: Haar-Baire Wave*
  Classical any-angle planners propagate geometry through grids:
    Field D* interpolates; Theta* shortcuts by line of sight;
    Block A* caches local paths; ANYA uses interval/taut nodes;
    CWave propagates primitive wavefront arcs and lines.
  Proposed proof planner:
    Haar-Baire Wave* propagates Borel interval fronts on the circle/subtorus,
    labelled by (strict Haar mass, Baire interior, closed boundary support).
  LRC use:
    line of sight  -> no unsafe arc blocks a witness interval;
    taut path      -> every heading change is a cover-arc boundary event;
    wavefront      -> exact denominator combs and wall crossings;
    Haar label     -> canonical invariant mass on the orbit-closure torus;
    Baire label    -> open/nonmeager interval versus meager boundary support.

